{"strongs": "H3091", "word": "יְהוֺשׁוּעַ", "translit": "ye.ho.shu.a", "root": "יה", "morph": "N:N-M-P", "pos": "proper name, masculine", "gloss": "in south of Judah", "definition": "יְהוֺשׁוּעַ , יְהוֺשֻׁעַ and (later) יֵשׁוּעַ , proper name, masculine (& location, see 9 below) ( ׳ י is salvation , or ׳ י is opulence , compare אֱלִישָׁע , אֱלִישׁוּעַ , אֲבִישׁוּעַ & Nes SK 1892, 573 f. ; in any case it came to be associated with ישׁע , compare Matt 1:21 on יֵשׁוּעַ see especially Frä VOJ iv. 1890, 332 f. Müll SK 1892, 177 f. who cite analogue for change of וֹ to later ֵ֯ , & Nes l.c .) — 1. Moses' successor, son of Nun, ( ᵐ5 Ἰησοῦς ) יְהוֺשׁוּעַ Deut 3:21 ; Judg 2:7 = יְהוֺשֻׁעַ Exod 17:9 ; Exod 17:10 ; Exod 17:13 ; Exod 17:14 ; Exod 24:13 ; Exod 32:17 ; Exod 33:11 ; Num 11:28 ; Num 13:16 ; Num 14:6 ; Num 14:30 ; Num 14:38 ; Num 26:65 ; Num 27:18 ; Num 27:22 ; Num 32:12 ; Num 32:28 ; Num 34:17 ; Deut 1:38 ; Deut 3:28 ; Deut 31:3 ; Deut 31:7 ; Deut 31:14 (twice in verse); Deut 31:23 ; Deut 34:9 ; Josh 1:1 + 167 t. Joshua; Judg 1:1 ; Judg 2:6 ; Judg 2:7 ; Judg 2:8 ; Judg 2:21 ; Judg 2:23 ; 1Kgs 16:34 ; 1Chr 7:27 = יֵשׁוּעַ Neh 8:17 ( ᵐ5 Ἰησοῦς ); according to P , name changed by Moses from הוֺשֵׁעַ q. v. Num 13:8 ; Num 13:16 ( ᵐ5 Αὑση ) Deut 32:44 ( ᵐ5 Ἰησοῦς ). 2. יְהוֺשֻׁעַ a Bethshemite 1Sam 6:14 ; 1Sam 6:18 ( ᵐ5 'Wshe , A Ἰησοῦς , ᵐ5 L Ἰωσηε ). 3. high priest after the restoration, son of Jehozadak יְהוֺשֻׁעַ ( ᵐ5 Ἰησοῦς ) Hag 1:1 ; Hag 1:12 ; Hag 1:14 ; Hag 2:2 ; Hag 2:4 ; Zech 3:1 ; Zech 3:3 ; Zech 3:6 ; Zech 3:8 ; Zech 3:9 ; Zech 6:11 = יְשׁוּעַ ( ᵐ5 Ἰησοῦς ) Ezra 2:2 ; Ezra 3:2 ; Ezra 3:8 ; Ezra 4:3 ; Ezra 5:2 ; Ezra 10:18 ; Neh 7:7 ; Neh 12:1 ; Neh 12:7 ; Neh 12:10 ; Neh 12:26 . 4. יְהוֺשֻׁעַ governor of Jerusalem under Josiah 2Kgs 23:8 ( ᵐ5 Ἰησοῦς , ᵐ5 L Ἰωσηε ). 5. יֵשׁוּעַ ( ᵐ5 Ἰησοῦς ). head of one of the classes of priests 1Chr 24:11 , possibly also Ezra 2:36 = Neh 7:39 . 6. יֵשׁוּעַ ( ᵐ5 Ἰησοῦς etc.), a Levitical family-name of frequent occurrence: \\ \\ a. Ezra 2:40 ; Ezra 3:9 = Neh 7:43 ; Neh 8:7 ; Neh 9:4 ; Neh 9:5 ; Neh 10:10 ; Neh 12:8 . \\ \\ b. 2Chr 31:15 ; Ezra 8:33 ; Neh 12:24 . 7. יֵשׁוּעַ ( ᵐ5 id. ), father of a builder at the wall Neh 3:19 , perhaps = 8. a Judaite family-name ( ᵐ5 id. ), Ezra 2:6 = Neh 7:11 (compare Sm Listen 12 ). 9. proper name, of a location in south of Judah Neh 11:26 בְּיֵשׁוּעַ ( ᵐ5 ἐν Ἰησού , ᵐ5 L ἐν Σουα ).", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2120')\">BDB2120</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H3091')\">H3091</entry> <entry onclick=\"sn('H3442')\">H3442</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2119')\">BDB2119</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2121')\">BDB2121</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>יְהוֺשׁוּעַ</bdbheb>, <bdbheb>יְהוֺשֻׁעַ</bdbheb> and (later) <bdbheb>יֵשׁוּעַ</bdbheb>, <b>proper name, masculine</b> (&amp; location, see <b>9</b> below) (<bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>י</bdbheb> <highlight>is salvation</highlight>, or <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>י</bdbheb> <highlight>is opulence</highlight>, compare <bdbheb>אֱלִישָׁע</bdbheb>, <bdbheb>אֱלִישׁוּעַ</bdbheb>, <bdbheb>אֲבִישׁוּעַ</bdbheb> &amp; <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Nes')\">Nes<sup>SK 1892, 573 f.</sup></lookup>; in any case it came to be associated with <bdbheb>ישׁע</bdbheb>, compare <ref ref=\"Matt 1:21\" b=\"40\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"21\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"21\" onclick=\"bcv(40,1,21)\">Matt 1:21</ref> on <bdbheb>יֵשׁוּעַ</bdbheb> see especially <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Frä')\">Frä<sup>VOJ iv. 1890, 332 f.</sup></lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Müll')\">Müll<sup>SK 1892, 177 f.</sup></lookup> who cite analogue for change of <bdbheb>וֹ</bdbheb> to later <bdbheb>ֵ֯</bdbheb>, &amp; <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Nes')\">Nes<sup>l.c</sup></lookup>.) — <div class=\"point\"><b>1.</b> Moses' successor, son of Nun, (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Sept')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵐ5</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> <grk>Ἰησοῦς</grk>) <bdbheb>יְהוֺשׁוּעַ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Deut 3:21\" b=\"5\" cBegin=